<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <title></title>
    <link type="text/css" rel="stylesheet" href="../assets/QRCode/Styles/page.css" />
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="container-heading1">
            <h1 class="heading1">Introduction</h1>
            <p class="mrg-t-4">
                We are delighted to announce the launch of a new function "<strong>Create Member with QR code</strong>". Not only does it support the creation of a new member account quickly, it also helps member to log into the member site and start the experience immediately.
            </p>

            <h1 class="heading1">Create new Member account via QR code </h1>
            <div class="container-heading2">
                <h2 class="heading2"><span class="step">Step 1: </span>Access to the new function for creating a new account, you can do this in 3 ways: </h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        Top right menu.
                        <div class="img-box"><img src="../assets/QRCode/Styles/Images/en/1.png" /></div>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Add new Member page (QR Code tab).
                        <div class="img-box"><img src="../assets/QRCode/Styles/Images/en/2.png" /></div>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Account Info (next to the member’s username).
                        <div class="img-box"><img src="../assets/QRCode/Styles/Images/en/3.png" /></div>
                    </li>
                </ul>

                <h2 class="heading2"><span class="step">Step 2: </span>Fill in the information.</h2>
                <div class="img-box"><img src="../assets/QRCode/Styles/Images/en/4.png" /></div>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        In case you access this function by clicking the <img src="../assets/QRCode/Styles/Images/copy.png"/> icon on the Account Info, the <i>Existing Member account</i> and <i>Member Credit</i> fields will be automatically filled in with the corresponding data.
                    </li>
                </ul>
                <h2 class="heading2"><span class="step">Step 3: </span>Select a domain url and complete the account creation process.</h2>
                <div class="img-box"><img src="../assets/QRCode/Styles/Images/en/5.png" /></div>
                <p>At this point, Member can scan this QR code directly (recommended), or you can send them the QR code manually by clicking on the "<strong>Copy link</strong>”. Either way will help Member to reach the Member site and here they will be forced to change the password (for security purposes).</p>
                <p>
                    You can also edit Member’s info such as First Name, Last Name, Mobile Phone, etc. or their given credit amount by clicking on the <strong>Update Information</strong> button or <strong>Update Given Credit</strong> button:
                </p>
                <div class="img-box"><img src="../assets/QRCode/Styles/Images/en/6.png" /></div>
                <div class="img-box"><img src="../assets/QRCode/Styles/Images/en/7.png" /></div>
            </div>
            <h1 class="heading1">Notes</h1>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    Once an account has been successfully created, for the next use, the <i>Existing Member account</i> and <i>Member Credit</i> fields (in step 2) will be automatically filled in with the previous account data.
                </li>
                <li>
                    In a day, you can create up to 200 member accounts using this method. After reaching that number, the message <i>"You can only create up to 200 new members every day by this function"</i> will be displayed if you click on the <strong>Create Account</strong> button.
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>